id: SECRETS-054
title: Auth0 Client Secret
category: secrets
severity: error
engine: pattern
target:
  extensions: .ts .tsx .js .jsx .py .java .go .rb .rs .cpp .h .cs .php .env .yml .yaml .json .toml .xml .properties .cfg .ini .conf .sh .tf .hcl
  exclude_paths: test/ vendor/ node_modules/ .git/ build/ dist/ __pycache__/ .venv/ target/
  content_contains: auth0
patterns:
  - regex: [A-Za-z0-9_-]{32,}
    message: Auth0 client secret detected. This allows impersonation of your application to the Auth0 authorization server.
fix: Rotate the secret at Auth0 Dashboard > Applications > Settings. Store the new secret in environment variables and use it only server-side.
